.TH TIGRIS\-DIFF 8 "7 October 2026" "Tigris 3.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tigris\-diff \- what changed between two Tigris runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tigris\-diff
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR logdir ]
.RI [ old.jsonl " [" new.jsonl ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tigris\-diff
compares the JSON Lines reports of two runs of
.BR tigris (8)
and lists the findings that are new in the second and the ones that
were resolved since the first. A finding is the same finding when its
level, id and message are the same.
.LP
With no files, the two most recent runs in the log directory are
compared; with one, that run and the one before it.
.LP
A new finding that is already accepted
.RB ( tigris\-accept (8))
is listed, marked so, and does not count as new. A check skipped in
either run (it needed root, or could not read an offline root) is left
out of both sides, so that a skip is not taken for a fix. When the runs
used different configurations, profiles or roots, the output says so,
since a check on in only one of them shows its findings as new or
resolved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Include INFO findings, which are left out by default.
.TP
.B \-j
Write the result as one JSON object instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-l " logdir"
The log directory: by default
.I ./log
if it exists, else
.IR /var/log/tiger .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing new is open.
.TP
.B 1
Something new is open.
.TP
.B 2
An error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
tigris\-diff                       # the last two runs
tigris\-diff old.jsonl new.jsonl   # any two
.fi
.RE
.LP
.B tigris \-\-since last
does the same as part of a run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tigris (8),
.BR tigris\-accept (8)
